I earlier posted about a "missing resource" error for the unofficial
Mac Binaries from ftp.uu.net that prevented the program from starting up.

The problem is not with System 7.1, but rather NowMenus 3.0.2.  I don't
know if this problem is specific to my unofficial copy of the game or whether
the problem will persist in the official version.  Removing NowMenus
and rebooting will allow NetHack 3.1 to run SUPERBLY on my Mac IIsi.

Kudos to the development team for adding so much new dimension to an
already addictive game!


